Chapter: ConstraintOrdGeneric
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 A generic function constrained by `Ord a =>` can call `compare` on its
 type parameter. compare is two-argument, so dispatch threads the
 concrete type's derived `__compare_T` through the curried application.

Section: Types

  Shape =
    | Circle (Integer)
    | Rect (Integer) (Integer)
    deriving Ord

Section: Body

  rel : Ord a => a -> a -> Text
  rel (x) (y) =
    let c = compare x y
    in if c < 0 then "lt" else if c > 0 then "gt" else "eq"

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (rel (Circle 1) (Circle 2))
    print-line-uni (rel (Circle 5) (Circle 5))
    print-line-uni (rel (Rect 3 4) (Circle 9))
  end

